Well a couple of months ago, the general consensus was to
NOT start adding more weapons to the game.  We've already got
a lot of them, and many people would favor a game which didn't
go any further in the direction of hack and slay.  In fact,
as it is, many experienced players think that the game already
gets boring beating on the deeper monsters with the weapons
we already have.  Adding new instruments of carnage would only
mean yet-another-thing-to-hack-the-Wiz with.

On the contrary, since the spread of 3.1, I've seen many
posts that even suggest Decreasing the Artifact weapons in the
game.  After all, if not everyone can get a named weapon
without a wish, your spellcasters might actually be forced
to (gasp) cast spells!

I think the biggest draw of Nethack is all the neato side things
that you have.  Scrolls, potions, wands, altars, spells, pets,
quests, etc.  Many of these serve to prevent the game from
being a huge exercise in hack-and-slay.  Blindly adding every
weapon from every fiction ever written (let alone 12 swords
from a single source) would tend to defeat this trend.

IMHO, of course.

